    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "UNITED\nAIRLINES\nFLY THE MAIN LINE\nThe Pioneer Coast-to-Coast Airway\nEffective December 1, 1937",
      "An unmatched record of 125,000,000 miles experience\nTO ALASKA\nVANCOUVER\nC A\nORIENT\nTO THE\nORIEN\nSEATTLE\nTACOMA\nRainier\nPORTLAND•\n• SPOKANE\nWALLA\nWALLA\nTENDLETON\nBUTT\nMEDFORD\nBOSe\nCLAND\nGlacier\nTOREAT ALS\nHELENA\nYellowstone\n•\nGrand\nTeton\nDude\nRanches\n; ROCK SPRINGS\nCHEYENNE\nWINNIPEG O\nMONTREAL\nMINNEAPOLIS\nST PAUL\nBOSTON\nMILWAUKEE\nCAGO.\nCLEVELAND\nTO HAWAII\n→ THE ORIENT\nSAN FRANCISCO\nSACRAMENTO\nRENO\nYosemite\nFRESNO\nERSFIELD\nOMAHA\nLINCULN\nDES\nMOINES\nCLAU\nSALY\nEstes\nPark\nCedar\nBreaks\nLAKE\nzion\nBoulder Dam\nDENVER\n) COLORADO SPRINGS\nMADISON\nIOWA\nMOLINE\nST. LOUIS\nTOLEDG\n/NEW YORK\nPHILADELPHIA\nBALTIMOR!\nCAMDEN\nWASHINGTON\nKANSAS CITY\nLOUISVILLE\nPITTSBURG\nINCINNATI\nWICHIT\nGrand Canyon\nTO HAWAI\nSANTA RARRARA\nLOS ANGELES\nLONG BEACH\nSAN DIEGO\nNASHVILLE\nCHATTANOOGI\nPHOENIX\nCHARLESTON\nJACKSON\nMONTGOMERY\nfly the\nMAIN\nLINE\nThe Only Airway Linking the\nEast with Every Major\nPacific Coast City\nHOUSEU\nGALVESTON(\n• UNITED AIR LINES\nST. PETERSBURG\nConnecting Air Lines\n# Rail Lines •..... Highways\n• National Parks\nTo Cuba, Central and\nuth America\nUNITED AIR LINES' central Mid-Continent route\nis by ten years the oldest coast-to-coast airway. It\nwas selected by government airway engineers in 1919\nas the most suitable transcontinental air route.\nIt parallels the famous Overland Trail, for more than\na century the principal route of coast-to-coast trans-\nportation. The Covered Wagons of 1830 crossed the\ngreat plains to the Pacific Coast along the Overland\nTrail. Today, more than ever, this central route across\nthe continent is the Main Line-and over it United flies\nmore traffic ton miles than are flown on any other long\ndistance airway in the world.\nOnly United Flies the Famous\nSkylounge Mainliner.\nUnited's Cuisine is a Main Line\nFeature.\nThis airway was first to have plane-ground radio com-\nmunication, first to be lighted for night flying, first\nto have weather reporting service, first to have radio\nrange facilities. The central Mid-continent airway\nrepresents outstanding developments in airline facil-\nities, and as such, it has been studied by experts\nof airlines and governments the world over.\nTO EUROP\nPAGE 1"
    ],
